+// The grip of a handshake: the thumb over the partner's back, then the long fingers closed around
+// the little-finger edge of the partner's hand onto its back. 'open': the spreads and the starting
+// flexions; 'forearm': one's forearm direction from the wrist (hand frame), the partner's being the
+// same in its own frame. Right-hand convention (the values suit either hand).
+inline FingerPose solveShakeGrip(const Skeleton& sk, float pitch, vec3 anchor, vec3 forearm, const FingerPose& open) {
+    const mat4 partner = shakePartner(pitch, anchor), toPartner = inverseAffine(partner);
